OL,3,GNEWSAThe 101-year-old who is older than
OL,4,Athe place where she lives
OL,5,
OL,6,FWhen Kathleen Cotton moved to
OL,7,FWythenshawe in the 1950s, it was
OL,8,Fquieter than she thought it would be.
OL,10,FHer husband, a serving police officer
OL,11,Fin Manchester at the time, had been
OL,12,Foffered a house in the area so they
OL,13,Fdecided to relocate about 10 miles from
OL,14,Ftheir home in Openshaw.
OL,16,FThis marked the start of her life in
OL,17,FWythenshawe and helped to shape the
OL,18,Fperson she is today as she approaches
OL,19,Fher 102nd birthday.
OL,23,APub: 19-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
